Cell["Only the relative cat-state phase \[Phi] is varied. The \
coherent-amplitude phase \[CurlyPhi] remains Pi/2. Fixed parameters: m = r = \
1, delta1 = Pi/2; s = {0, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 1.0}. The original delta2 sampling \
is retained. All three plots use the same axes.", "Text", 
      ExpressionUUID -> "c625ce0d-7d9a-462d-b25d-1459ff5f8537"],

Cell["For these parameters, every curve passes through (delta2 = Pi/2, \
Ps = 1/2). At the sampled nonzero couplings, even > Yurke-Stoler > odd for \
delta2 > Pi/2; the order reverses for delta2 < Pi/2. The s = 0 curve is \
identical for all three states. Here m = r = 1 makes the Yurke-Stoler \
probability the arithmetic mean of the even and odd cases. 'Photon-added \
even/odd' names the parent cat: one photon addition reverses its \
photon-number parity.", "Text", ExpressionUUID -> 
       "e87de0bf-ec20-4508-8a62-f5d4838040e1"],

